      <h2>Credits</h2>

      <p><em>The Heir</em> owes a lot to the mods that came before it. Its candidate selection system adapts the Republican side of <em>Things That Never Were</em>. The opposing party always fields the same candidate, but their campaign changes in response to your actions, as in <em>All The Way</em>. The economic system was inspired by <em>Our Revolution</em>. I also used code from <em>Hope</em> and <em>Little Big Man</em> for the achievements, list of presidents, and cabinet, and from <em>An Old Cycle</em> for the Spotify window. Special thanks to Strawberry Master for that code, as well as for the County Map, data visualizer, and Campaign Polling History. Thanks also to mangolith, thatchmaster, Literally Nelson Rockefeller, ItsAstronomics, and Jet for the Modding Tool. Go play their games, too. You’ll probably enjoy them as much as mine, if not more.</p>

      <p>But the biggest help in making this mod was undoubtedly ChatGPT and its Codex tool. I should disclose that most of the game’s code was generated by AI. It also helped me translate the endings, since English isn’t my first language. The text you’re reading right now was translated by AI. I also used it to age some of the portraits in the list of presidents. I think this little tool is going to change the world and make countless things easier for us. I understand why some people are wary of it, but to me, fighting it is like fighting the arrow of time.</p>
    `
